 "subject": "graph,store,cli,mcp: index the hot lookups, sort the snapshots",
 "body": "Perf, all edge-set-neutral (flask/gin/guava edge dumps byte-identical\nto before), plus the determinism holes the same code paths exposed.\n\nCodeGraph gains a byName index built once per install, replacing the\nscan-all-70k-symbols-then-sort that opened ChangeImpact,\nMissingImplementations, hasIndexedType and the bare-name resolver.\nNeighbors' \"out\" branch scanned the entire edge list to find one\nsymbol's out-edges while the \"in\" branch beside it already used the\ninbound index; it now uses outbound. ComputeICR called Deps \u2014 an\nO(all-edges) prefix scan \u2014 once per seed, and Search returns 20 seeds\nthat routinely share a file; it now scans once per unique file.\n\nimportFilesForQualifier is memoized per (file, qualifier) in a\nsync.Map (the parallel call workers share it) and no longer allocates\na Split slice plus a Join string per import segment per call site, nor\nrecomputes \"/\"+impNorm inside two whole-table loops. Measured on\nguava: edge/calls 1.74s -> 1.72s \u2014 smaller than hoped, so this is\nrecorded as an allocation win, not a speedup claim.\n\nAllSymbols/AllEdges/EdgesBySource preallocate from a COUNT(*) instead\nof doubling a 600k-element slice ~20 times. The count is taken BEFORE\nthe row",
